+    "**Cross-PCF** measures whether two cell types occur near one another more or less frequently than expected given the observed tissue structure. We retain the measured cell locations and compare the observed cell-type arrangement with a random-labelling null model, this separates cell-type co-localisation from effects caused by tissue boundaries, holes, fragmentation, or other irregular spatial geometry.\n",
