+    "## Comparing full interaction curves using divergence"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "f8157223",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Previously, we used AUC to collapse each interaction curve into a single number. This is simple and useful for ranking, but it discards where along radius r two curves differ. In addition, differences with opposite signs at different radii can cancel when summarized by a signed integral.\n",
+    "<br>\n",
+    "Here, we introduce a second summary score that compares the **full curves**: curve divergence.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Unlike `AUC–log2`, divergence does not describe whether an interaction is generally enriched or depleted. Instead, it answers:\n",
+    "> How different are these two spatial interaction profiles, and at what radius is their separation greatest?\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**Read it as:** divergence `≈ 0` means the two interactions have similar spatial profiles, while a larger value means they differ more strongly across distance.\n"
    ]
   },
   {
    "cell_type": "code",
-   "execution_count": 21,
-   "id": "023a0c71",
